# Keep the Docker build context small. Without this, "COPY . ." ships ~530MB,
# of which _build alone is ~463MB and .git another ~34MB - none of it useful,
# since the Dockerfile builds from source anyway. It also means every local
# dune build invalidates the COPY layer and re-runs the whole image build.
#
# CAUTION: this file does NOT use .gitignore syntax. Patterns are matched with
# Go's filepath.Match against the path relative to the context root, so:
#   - a bare pattern matches only at the TOP level; in .gitignore the same
#     pattern would match at any depth. Hence the "**/" prefixes below - the
#     214 .md5sum_* files live in asm/, ir/ and friends, not at the root, so
#     a bare ".md5sum_*" would match none of them.
#   - "*" does not cross "/".
#   - there is no "!" un-ignore ordering subtlety worth relying on here, so
#     the list is kept purely additive.
#
# NB: bin/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is a checked-in symlink to
# _build/install/default/bin, so it arrives dangling and is resolved by the
# "dune build @install" step - exactly as in a fresh clone.
#
# NB: tests/tiger/*.o and *.a are deliberately NOT excluded either. Those
# prebuilt i386 artifacts are checked in and are what the behavioural test
# suite links against.

# dune output
**/_build

# version control
.git

**/*.cm*

# build directories of the demos, the run-time system and the test runners
demos/build
runtime/build
tests/build

# syncweb bookkeeping
**/.md5sum_*
**/*.nwcache

# editor and OS cruft
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
